===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A [[state]] or situation of great [[confusion]], [[disorder]], [[trouble]] or [[destruction]]; [[chaos]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:disorder|Thesaurus:commotion}}
#: {{ux|en|What if the legendary hero Robin Hood had been born into the '''mayhem''' of the 20th century?}}
#: {{ux|en|In all the '''mayhem''', some children were separated from their parents.}}
#* {{RQ:London Iron Heel|passage=“Tell me,” I said, “when one surrenders his personal feelings to his professional feelings, may not the action be defined as a sort of spiritual '''mayhem'''?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author=Anton Szandor La Vey|title=Satan Speaks!|text=Available in an instant, it can be firmly grasped and employed to scrape, gouge, rake, and generally wreak '''mayhem''' on any pest who accelerates into assaultive status.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Emma Trevayne|title=Flights and Chimes and Mysterious Times|text=Jack lifted the binoculars to his eyes, and it was difficult not to laugh at the utter '''mayhem'''. Faeries ripped plumes from helmets; soldiers found their pistols dangled just out of reach.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Kari Paul|title=Robotaxi breakdowns cause mayhem in San Francisco days after expansion vote|work=The Guardian|date=2023-08-14|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/san-francisco-robotaxi-waymo-cruise-breakdown|issn=0261-3077|passage=One TikTok user recorded a Cruise vehicle causing “'''mayhem'''” outside of the festival where it was stuck at an angle in the middle of the street.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Matthew Weaver|title=‘Absolute mayhem’: Eurostar passengers tell of stress and tears|work=The Guardian|date=2023-12-31|url=https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/dec/31/absolute-mayhem-eurostar-passengers-tell-of-stress-and-tears|issn=0261-3077|passage=Andrew and Fiona Eyre, both 52, from Sheffield, had been looking forward to their trip to Paris since booking it in September, but their train was also cancelled. “It was absolute '''mayhem''' and the lack of communication was just disgusting,” Andrew said.}}
# Infliction of violent [[injury]] on a person or thing.
#: {{ux|en|The fighting dogs created '''mayhem''' in the flower beds.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain Roughing It|passage= This same man{{...|, after failing through intimidation to elicit from me the names of our editorial contributors, against giving which he knew me to be pledged,}} beat himself weary upon me with a raw hide, I not resisting, and then pantingly threatened me with permanent disfiguring '''mayhem''', if ever again I should introduce his name into print {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[maim]]ing of a person by depriving him of the use of any of his limbs which are necessary for defense or protection.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1912|title=Courts and Criminals|author=w:Arthur Cheney Train|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/5268/pg5268-images.html|passage=There is a story told of a case where a notorious character was charged with the unusual crime of “'''mayhem'''”—biting off another man's finger. The defendant's counsel secured adjournment after adjournment—no one knew why.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[crime]] of [[damaging]] things or [[harming]] people on purpose.

